Patch from MiniMyth2 project

Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>



From f77358810026d6aa8592ba2398722af4608ebd15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:39:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] media: amlogic: amvdec: don't touch a powered-down HEVC
 core when the DMC park fails

__vdec_hevc_start() parks the HEVC DMC request ports before it powers the
HEVC memories and resets the core. When the park timed out, the error
path called __vdec_hevc_stop(), which writes HEVC_ASSIST_MBOX1_MASK, halts
the AMRISC and quiesces the core. With the memories still powered down
those accesses hard-lock the SoC (seen on SC2, whose DMC idle status is
not where the S4 one is).

Back out only what was done before the park: unpark, power the HEVC
domain down again and disable the clock, then return the error. The
session start fails and the other decoder core keeps working.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .../platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c     | 20 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c
index 14f8a84..6eefe7e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c
@@ -446,7 +446,7 @@ static int __vdec_hevc_start(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	 */
 	ret = amvdec_hevc_dmc_park(core);
 	if (ret)
-		goto stop;
+		goto park_failed;
 
 	if (core->pd_list) {
 		/* Power the memories before the reset, and hold the reset */
@@ -519,6 +519,24 @@ stop:
 	if (!__vdec_hevc_stop(sess))
 		clk_disable_unprepare(core->amvdec_hevc_clk);
 	return ret;
+
+park_failed:
+	/*
+	 * The HEVC memories are still powered down and the core has not been
+	 * reset: __vdec_hevc_stop() would access HEVC registers and lock up
+	 * the SoC. Undo only the power-up done so far.
+	 */
+	amvdec_hevc_dmc_unpark(core);
+	if (core->pd_list)
+		meson_amvdec_power_domain_off(core, AMVDEC_PD_HEVC);
+	else if (core->platform->revision == AMVDEC_REVISION_SM1)
+		regmap_update_bits(core->regmap_ao, AO_RTI_GEN_PWR_SLEEP0,
+				   GEN_PWR_VDEC_HEVC_SM1, GEN_PWR_VDEC_HEVC_SM1);
+	else
+		regmap_update_bits(core->regmap_ao, AO_RTI_GEN_PWR_SLEEP0,
+				   GEN_PWR_VDEC_HEVC, GEN_PWR_VDEC_HEVC);
+	clk_disable_unprepare(core->amvdec_hevc_clk);
+	return ret;
 }
 
